  "result": "New issue numbers are set in `src/server/repositories/issue-repository.ts`, by the `nextIssueNumber(orgId, projectId)` function (around line 292).\n\nIt looks up the highest issue number among that organization's issues in that project, then adds 1. If the project has no issues yet, it returns 1, which is why each project starts again at 1. Archived issues are included in the lookup, so their numbers are never given out again.\n\n`src/server/services/issue-service.ts:68` calls this function and passes the result to `insertIssue`. It uses the number but doesn't work it out, so I left it out of the answer.\n\nANSWER: src/server/repositories/issue-repository.ts",
